## Ecosystem official name

Rather than treating them as three unrelated projects, they should be presented as:

# The Phoenix Ecosystem

```text
                 THE PHOENIX ECOSYSTEM

        🔥 Phoenix Forge
        Intelligent Asset Authoring
                 │
                 ▼
        🏛️ Phoenix Builder
      Procedural Architectural Assembly
                 │
                 ▼
         🎮 Phoenix Engine
         Runtime & Simulation
```

This also leaves room for future tools without breaking the naming convention.

For example:

* 🧪 **Phoenix Lab** → experimental features and procedural generators.
* 📦 **Phoenix Vault** → online repository for Building Kits, Material Vaults, Templates and community assets.
* 🌍 **Phoenix World** → future district/city/world editor.
* 📖 **Phoenix Atlas** → documentation, examples and learning hub.

Whether those ever exist or not, the ecosystem already feels scalable.

---

## Something I'd like to make an official architectural principle

I'd even add this to the Design Bible later as a formal decision:

> **Every Phoenix application should have a single, clearly defined responsibility.**

| Application         | Responsibility            | Does NOT do                 |
| ------------------- | ------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| 🔥 Phoenix Forge    | Create intelligent assets | Build complete architecture |
| 🏛️ Phoenix Builder | Assemble architecture     | Model arbitrary geometry    |
| 🎮 Phoenix Engine   | Simulate and render games | Author assets               |

That single principle will help prevent feature creep across all three projects.

